---
import LegalPage from '~/components/layout/LegalPage.astro';
import PlayCta from '~/components/article/PlayCta.astro';
import HeroArt from '~/components/art/HeroArt.astro';
import { getUi } from '~/i18n/ui';
import { defaultLocale } from '~/i18n/routing';
import { site } from '~/config/site';
import { contactEmail } from '~/lib/contact-email';

const labels = getUi(defaultLocale).shared.visuals;
const email = contactEmail();
---

<LegalPage
  locale={defaultLocale}
  title="About"
  description="Who runs Rarest Answer, how answer lists and guides are made, and what this independent trivia site does not claim."
  lastUpdated="2026-11-15"
>
  <aside slot="illustration" class="content-band mt-6">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <p class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug">{labels.aboutBand}</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{labels.aboutBandNote}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-band__art"><HeroArt /></div>
  </aside>
  <p>
    {site.name} is the home of {site.game.name}, a free daily trivia game you play in the browser.
    A prompt asks you to name something that fits. Every accepted answer is correct. A rarer correct
    answer scores higher than the name almost everyone types first.
  </p>
  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>
    A small independent team runs {site.name}. Guides and pages about other games are signed
    Rarest Answer editorial team. Article pages show that byline and link to this page. The name
    is this site's editorial group.
  </p>
  <p>
    {site.name} is not affiliated with Krillion or with the other games named on this site.
    {site.legalNotice}
  </p>
  <p>
    Questions and corrections go to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. That is the address
    on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>What you can do here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Play the shared daily round on the <a href="/">homepage</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Keep practicing in <a href="/unlimited/">unlimited mode</a>, or pick one category under trivia.
    </li>
    <li>
      Read the <a href="/guides/how-to-play-rarest-answer/">rules</a> and the
      <a href="/guides/how-to-find-rare-answers/">guide to finding a rare answer</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Compare other <a href="/guides/best-daily-trivia-games/">daily trivia games</a> and
      <a href="/games/">games like this one</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How a correct answer scores</h2>
  <p>
    Scores use six tiers. Common is 5 points, Familiar is 10, Uncommon is 20, Rare is 40, Epic is
    70, and Legendary is 100. Tier 6 is the rarest. Once each round, a Spotlight boost doubles the
    points for a single prompt. The full table and the difference between the daily round and
    unlimited play are on the <a href="/guides/how-to-play-rarest-answer/">how to play</a> page.
  </p>
  <h2>What this site is not</h2>
  <p>
    {site.game.name} is an independent game. Pages about other games, including Krillion and the
    Roblox experience Rarest Answer Party, are unofficial guides. They are not written by those
    creators, and they are not affiliated with them, with Roblox, or with the shows and puzzles
    they mention. {site.legalNotice}
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not invent codes, point tables, release dates, or creator names. If a public page does
    not state a rule, the guide says so instead of filling the gap. The
    <a href="/guides/rarest-answer-party-roblox/">Roblox page</a> quotes the experience description
    and a dated read of Roblox's games API. Live player counts on that page will move.
  </p>
  <h2>How we make this</h2>
  <p>
    Each prompt is a fixed list of accepted answers. Most lists come from Wikidata, which is
    published under CC0. English interjections come from Wikidata lexemes. The Stranger Things
    character list is parsed from the English Wikipedia page
    <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Stranger_Things_characters">List of Stranger Things characters</a>.
    On that list, a name with no English Wikipedia article is counted as 1 pageview.
  </p>
  <p>
    Rarity uses those pageview totals. The build script <code>scripts/build-prompts.ts</code> sums
    English Wikipedia pageviews over the last 12 complete months. English interjections use
    English Wiktionary pageviews for the same months. The files published now use November 2025
    through October 2026, labeled 2026-10 on each prompt. Running the script again refreshes the
    prompt files from those sources.
  </p>
  <p>
    Inside one prompt, rarity is a percentile of that total. The value runs from 0 to 1, and 1 is
    the rarest, the least viewed. Answers with the same total share a rarity. Tier cutoffs live in
    <code>scripts/data/prompt-defs.ts</code>: below 0.2 is Common, below 0.4 Familiar, below 0.6
    Uncommon, below 0.8 Rare, below 0.93 Epic, and 0.93 or higher is Legendary. Points for those
    tiers, 5, 10, 20, 40, 70, and 100, are the <code>TIERS</code> table in
    <code>src/lib/game/types.ts</code>. An answer is ranked only against the other answers to the
    same prompt.
  </p>
  <p>
    "Name a species of great ape" is one of those prompts: eight living species, with the Tapanuli
    orangutan in the rarest tier. The
    <a href="/guides/how-to-find-rare-answers/">finding guide</a> uses the names and the tier order,
    and it says when a biological fact comes from Wikipedia. The Stranger Things list is a scored
    prompt on the <a href="/answers/stranger-things-characters/">characters page</a>, ranked by
    those pageview totals.
  </p>
  <p>
    Answer pages are generated from the prompt files. The guides and the pages about other games
    are written with AI assistance. Facts in those articles are checked against the sources the
    page links: an official page, a Wikipedia article, a dated public API read, or this site's own
    rules and prompt files.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    You do not need an account to read the guides or to play. Streaks and round stats are stored in
    your browser. Write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or use the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
  <PlayCta slot="after" locale={defaultLocale} />
</LegalPage>
